                        "entry_id": "e7e2fa3d-4c22-38fe-907a-3468c825c481",
                        "glosses": [
                            "iemand die zichzelf dokter noemt of dokter wordt genoemd die wonderen zou kunnen verrichten, meestal een kwakzalver of bedrieger"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c5b637cb-6f76-4935-91ca-b028cf0e6523",
                                "sense_id": "66f4bb3c-27c9-3102-ba9a-9b3a812caafb",
                                "text": "Er is geen BIG-registratie voor wonderdokters."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "aa85c25f-22d9-4e74-b7d9-b836c4c4eb3f",
                        "source_entry_id": "e7e2fa3d-4c22-38fe-907a-3468c825c481",
                        "source_sense_id": "66f4bb3c-27c9-3102-ba9a-9b3a812caafb",
                        "target_lang_word": "charlatan",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "charlatan",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dcc94f79-1be9-32e2-bc92-b58d651ab659",
                                        "entry_id": "850ce793-d6ee-30cf-9184-c8833d7c89f5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A mountebank, someone who addresses crowds in the street; (especially), an itinerant seller of medicines or drugs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b3787e75-6073-4b0b-acff-ed7542fddd58",
                                                "sense_id": "dcc94f79-1be9-32e2-bc92-b58d651ab659",
                                                "text": "The poor foreigner, more dead than alive, answered that he was an Italian charlatan, who had practised with some reputation in Padua […]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5d4d64de-58dc-3e55-a6c3-2001492daaba",
                                        "entry_id": "850ce793-d6ee-30cf-9184-c8833d7c89f5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A malicious trickster; a fake person, especially one who deceives for personal profit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c77977ef-a85b-4a06-8b74-9d3096bc60f7",
                                                "sense_id": "5d4d64de-58dc-3e55-a6c3-2001492daaba",
                                                "text": "“If there’s something you don’t understand,” urged Dr. Breed, “ask Dr. Horvath to explain it. He’s very good at explaining.” He turned to me. “Dr. Hoenikker used to say that any scientist who couldn’t explain to an eight-year-old what he was doing was a charlatan.”\n“Then I’m dumber than an eight-year-old,” Miss Pefko mourned. “I don’t even know what a charlatan is.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71aa59e1-cbcd-4a39-9d87-a52dc713e0e4",
                                                "sense_id": "5d4d64de-58dc-3e55-a6c3-2001492daaba",
                                                "text": "That this disgraceful charlatan holds one of the great offices of state in this country should be a source of constant shame and embarrassment to the Prime Minister."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b78a384c-c6f5-4068-9b55-ed9cb4bfbfe4",
                        "source_entry_id": "e7e2fa3d-4c22-38fe-907a-3468c825c481",
                        "source_sense_id": "66f4bb3c-27c9-3102-ba9a-9b3a812caafb",
                        "target_lang_word": "imposter",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "imposter",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "80a25230-e906-3e6b-a255-cca7584920fb",
                                        "entry_id": "c53227ab-3af7-3709-8bcc-85eb895587a1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative spelling of impostor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3cf1582a-ae6b-4842-8479-05bd4acf766c",
                                                "sense_id": "80a25230-e906-3e6b-a255-cca7584920fb",
                                                "text": "To get over her imposter syndrome, Caldwell eventually turned to guided meditation to help her \"quiet the voices.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "69ef8961-40b1-4ced-ad60-b2d954736a81",
                                                "sense_id": "80a25230-e906-3e6b-a255-cca7584920fb",
                                                "text": "The game requires four to 10 players, who are randomly assigned roles of either a crewmate or imposter. There are always more crew than imposters at the start."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d299be94-b4e5-4238-a427-24ab1a8dd98d",
                        "source_entry_id": "e7e2fa3d-4c22-38fe-907a-3468c825c481",
                        "source_sense_id": "66f4bb3c-27c9-3102-ba9a-9b3a812caafb",
                        "target_lang_word": "quack",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "quack",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c9210f85-2407-33ee-827c-bd6f7220d886",
                                        "entry_id": "19ccaa08-f036-35a1-a1a8-4a71d41d01e9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The sound made by a duck."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "143adf5b-8e26-4aa4-ae65-c364c2af08a4",
                                                "sense_id": "c9210f85-2407-33ee-827c-bd6f7220d886",
                                                "text": "Did you hear that duck make a quack?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "quack",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "168e99f4-a1f6-346b-b4ae-adf276571f86",
                                        "entry_id": "79c6851d-9124-3b20-a69d-da7714345091",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make a noise like a duck."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "13f1d58d-21bc-4d65-823e-650b51a53dbd",
                                                "sense_id": "168e99f4-a1f6-346b-b4ae-adf276571f86",
                                                "text": "The more breadcrumbs I threw on the ground, the more they quacked."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b5ba3b2-9be0-4b5b-88b9-fc1ce3a81fa0",
                                                "sense_id": "168e99f4-a1f6-346b-b4ae-adf276571f86",
                                                "text": "Do you hear the ducks quack?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9177e66f-9596-310e-a31a-12fd354cffcd",
                                        "entry_id": "79c6851d-9124-3b20-a69d-da7714345091",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a queen bee: to make a high-pitched sound during certain stages of development."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "quack",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "57bb6aa8-7f13-332c-a0ab-51d30714c33a",
                                        "entry_id": "494a5abf-75dd-3bfd-b9dc-096f85d033a4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A duck's quack."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "quack",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0c76647a-f77e-39a7-b80c-7a252684f6eb",
                                        "entry_id": "8c460593-8069-3523-89b5-38d36297f0e1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A fraudulent healer, especially a bombastic peddler in worthless treatments, a doctor who makes false diagnoses for monetary benefit, or an untrained or poorly trained doctor who uses fraudulent credentials to attract patients"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac8e470e-5c59-4a82-93c8-c2911c415795",
                                                "sense_id": "0c76647a-f77e-39a7-b80c-7a252684f6eb",
                                                "text": "That doctor is nothing but a lousy quack!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "babf4d63-2241-44bb-a8e3-898812eed2b3",
                                                "sense_id": "0c76647a-f77e-39a7-b80c-7a252684f6eb",
                                                "text": "1662, Rump: or an Exact Collection of the Choycest Poems and Songs Relating to Late Times, Vol. II, by ‘the most Eminent Wits’\nTis hard to say, how much these Arse-wormes do urge us, We now need no Quack but these Jacks for to purge us, …"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7fde91d8-efe9-479c-86a3-062c7dacdea9",
                                                "sense_id": "0c76647a-f77e-39a7-b80c-7a252684f6eb",
                                                "text": "After ſome Months, the Quack gets privately to Town, [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b28a00a3-0e65-449a-b6e9-110b71c83d5a",
                                                "sense_id": "0c76647a-f77e-39a7-b80c-7a252684f6eb",
                                                "text": "‘if we are ourselves valets, there shall ‘exist no hero for us; we shall not know the hero when we see him;’ - we shall take the quack for a hero; and cry, audibly through all ballot-boxes and machinery whatsoever, Thou art he; be thou King over us!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9695497e-2ad4-4433-8eb0-4a353e1ccf77",
                                                "sense_id": "0c76647a-f77e-39a7-b80c-7a252684f6eb",
                                                "text": "The advertising quack who wearies / With tales of countless cures, / His teeth, I've enacted, / Shall all be extracted / By terrified amateurs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a7f6481-b9f1-4767-9e91-8e261035bf7b",
                                                "sense_id": "0c76647a-f77e-39a7-b80c-7a252684f6eb",
                                                "text": "Polly (to security guard, referring to Dr. Feingarten): Are you going to let that shyster in there?\nDr. Feingarten: I could sue you, Polly. A shyster is a disreputable lawyer. I'm a quack."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df793d8e-3a79-4aef-8410-fe477278db64",
                                                "sense_id": "0c76647a-f77e-39a7-b80c-7a252684f6eb",
                                                "text": "\"I don't want to get into specifics, but when I was born, my parts were considered... ambiguous. The quack of a doctor that delivered me, had trouble assigning a gender. So at his recommendation - and surgical intervention - I was raised as a boy.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9fa690bc-8d3e-3d1f-8099-1aca5cb7be08",
                                        "entry_id": "8c460593-8069-3523-89b5-38d36297f0e1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any similar charlatan or incompetent professional."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a41800f-cfa8-4f3a-9459-a7bdefbadb17",
                                                "sense_id": "9fa690bc-8d3e-3d1f-8099-1aca5cb7be08",
                                                "text": "The very quaik of faſhions, the very hee that / VVeares a Steletto on his chinne."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6fd156a3-1f10-3307-a713-e274d2ce9a3f",
                                        "entry_id": "8c460593-8069-3523-89b5-38d36297f0e1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any doctor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "humorous",
                                            "mildly",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b70eb56c-ebcc-45c6-979b-7830a3f195dc",
                                                "sense_id": "6fd156a3-1f10-3307-a713-e274d2ce9a3f",
                                                "text": "That quack wants me to quit smoking, eat less, and start exercising. The nerve!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "quack",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e6a4b600-a378-32ec-af97-3eeb6aa3a646",
                                        "entry_id": "077433f4-eaa6-30f2-87a9-752a0bebc61b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To practice or commit quackery (fraudulent medicine)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98c20b27-85e7-441b-8393-a8e93155b095",
                                                "sense_id": "e6a4b600-a378-32ec-af97-3eeb6aa3a646",
                                                "text": "[…] it is incredible, and scarce to be imagin’d, how the Posts of Houses, and Corners of Streets were plaster’d over with Doctors Bills, and Papers of ignorant Fellows; quacking and tampering in Physick, and inviting the People to come to them for Remedies;"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b84f4f50-682f-3c12-8d06-1dbce5989204",
                                        "entry_id": "077433f4-eaa6-30f2-87a9-752a0bebc61b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make vain and loud pretensions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "504fcad3-4c95-467e-94a8-6c9f97fdc7d6",
                                                "sense_id": "b84f4f50-682f-3c12-8d06-1dbce5989204",
                                                "text": "Seek out for Plants with Signatures\nTo Quack of Universal Cures"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "quack",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3fd543a9-4f4a-35b7-afe9-90caf7b3ac49",
                                        "entry_id": "c443c00c-c4e2-3eb5-b1e6-2da999ef64d3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Falsely presented as having medicinal powers."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98f93066-bccb-4e49-9455-5c32a079b325",
                                                "sense_id": "3fd543a9-4f4a-35b7-afe9-90caf7b3ac49",
                                                "text": "Don't get your hopes up; that's quack medicine!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "103917ae-db3b-43cd-84f4-2c60edc41401",
                                                "sense_id": "3fd543a9-4f4a-35b7-afe9-90caf7b3ac49",
                                                "text": "In precisely the same way does a quack doctor prescribe his infallible nostrum to every patient, without taking into account differences of constitution, or [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27902a23-b31d-4d27-8f78-f01c01019553",
                                                "sense_id": "3fd543a9-4f4a-35b7-afe9-90caf7b3ac49",
                                                "text": "[R]ecently I examined as many newspapers and magazines as I could lay hands on just to see if I could find in them those old, alluring advertisements, ranging from the quack doctor to the quacker promoter and the quackest oracle of fate. There was nothing doing—everything as clean as a hound's tooth and as wholesome as sunshine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "81f30859-528c-4689-848d-2e6788661d07",
                                                "sense_id": "3fd543a9-4f4a-35b7-afe9-90caf7b3ac49",
                                                "text": "Finding, perhaps, that there is no solution either in politics or in any existing religion, he [the common man] may cling to the diagnosis of the last and quackest of his doctors: he may believe that art can save himself and the world."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9ac2fb8-8662-4b13-bbe0-2119b0558c8e",
                                                "sense_id": "3fd543a9-4f4a-35b7-afe9-90caf7b3ac49",
                                                "text": "When no certain cure exists, quack remedies tend to proliferate and the history of quackery and secret cures is full of extraordinary forms of treatment for the various arthritic disorders."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "095cb863-0b89-4703-a630-90d2406750fc",
                                                "sense_id": "3fd543a9-4f4a-35b7-afe9-90caf7b3ac49",
                                                "text": "They desperately want to believe something will help and for that reason they assist one another in obtaining unproven remedies. Such \"helpful\" promotion is generally more \"quack\" than fraudulent in nature."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5330e64e-0ff0-4266-80f1-9e216ba57980",
                                                "sense_id": "3fd543a9-4f4a-35b7-afe9-90caf7b3ac49",
                                                "text": "[William] Hogarth might have felt some sympathy for [Sally] Mapp as an 'irregular' expert besting pomposity, but this is topped by his sheer relish for her as the Quackest Quack of all, and female to boot. In Hogarth's print the dark goddess rules over her court of fools, men who have taken over the ancient realm of women's healing, and now profit from the people's ills and credulity."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
